From bb5482aa5486827deff4e7405f8cbe461a9f454a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 17:26:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Add HYPOTHESIS_ENGINE=hegel: libhegel as the engine
 behind core.py

With the environment variable set, core.py drives a test with HegelRunner
instead of ConjectureRunner whenever the backend is the default one. libhegel
owns the run loop, generation, targeting, shrinking and the choice budget;
Python keeps ConjectureData as the shim strategies draw from, the test
execution, interesting-origin bookkeeping and the final report. The runner
implements the subset of ConjectureRunner that core.py reads (counters,
interesting test cases, statistics, exit reason, new_conjecture_data) and
maps settings onto libhegel's: max_examples, phases, report_multiple_bugs,
suppressed health checks, and the seed from the settings-derived Random.

Each libhegel test case is executed through a draw-level provider bound to
that case; constant injection is off on this path so that every value the
test sees is a function of libhegel's draws, which its replays and shrinks
depend on. Span calls never raise on a case whose budget is spent, so
freezing an overrun ConjectureData closes its spans cleanly.

Not covered: the example database (libhegel's store is disabled and the
reuse phase skipped), the explain phase, and Hypothesis's own runner-level
health checks (libhegel's run instead). The discovery-ability quality tests
construct the runner directly and honour the flag too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
